}.$ Since the equation is written in standard form, we conclude that it is a first-order linear ODE.\n\nAll of the other equations cannot be written in the standard form, and therefore they are not first-order linear ODEs."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088419 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d8dc75e-3cf3-5795-857d-b484a8bface7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y=x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348706} {:answer/id #uuid "43bb70a4-1ebc-568d-ac4e-2b15cf3ae1b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+x=y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349062} {:answer/id #uuid "9c0edda0-970f-571f-af28-8b2bb516b055" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+x=y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349837} {:answer/id #uuid "aa32fc93-bb6e-5db9-9787-457ed8b63eb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y=xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349959} {:answer/id #uuid "f8e4844b-3007-5cd6-b780-6e847081831e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡{e}^{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({x}^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43bb70a4-1ebc-568d-ac4e-2b15cf3ae1b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+x=y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349062} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf81e7df-70d6-59a2-9d91-cf73151d372e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351070}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ecc44493-c978-58e2-96eb-083d048c8f5e" :question/math-academy-id "q-8352" :question/problem "Which of the following is **NOT** a first-order linear ordinary differential equation?" :question/worked-solution "To determine which of the following differential equations is a first-order linear ordinary differential equation, we attempt to write each option in the standard form.\n\nA first-order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x).\n$$\n\nLet's attempt to write $y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+x=y$ in the standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+x=y \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+x{y}^{-1}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis differential equation cannot be written in standard form since the power of $y$ in the term $x{y}^{-1}$ is not $1.$ Since the equation cannot be written in standard form, we conclude that it is not a first-order linear ODE.\n\nAll of the other equations can be written in the standard form, and therefore they are first-order linear ODEs."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238023 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f53d0fb-f21f-5d85-9b8f-a7a4b136209c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)y=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236015} {:answer/id #uuid "2ebad11d-35cc-5957-b0cd-d331da650b2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-xy={x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236113} {:answer/id #uuid "b02b6c4a-2dc7-5619-8048-51c5cb39616c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}+{x}^{2}y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236936} {:answer/id #uuid "b628a64b-bad4-555c-8a56-2de7f107366f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)=x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236969} {:answer/id #uuid "cd8ca442-9f52-5b49-8b9a-0d2e18880c58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-{x}^{3}y=\\frac{x}{1+y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237122}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f5